
  <sn><md>### Download a specifics files from github repo


Suppose the repository looks like this:

```text
Repository
├── README.md
├── images/
├── documents/
│   ├── book.pdf
│   ├── notes.txt
│   └── data.json
└── source/
```

To download only the `documents` folder:

```bash
git clone --no-checkout https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
cd REPOSITORY
git sparse-checkout init --cone
git sparse-checkout set documents
git checkout main
```

Your local folder will contain primarily:

```text
Repository/
├── README.md
└── documents/
    ├── book.pdf
    ├── notes.txt
    └── data.json
```
